# text = 遠く異朝をとぶらへば、秦の趙高、漢の王莽、梁の周伊、唐の禄山、是等は皆舊主先皇の政にもしたがはず、樂みをきはめ、諫をおもひいれず、天下のみだれむ事をさとらずして、民間の愁る所をしらざりしかば、久からずして亡じし者ども也。
# reading_translation = Looking far abroad to foreign lands, there were Zhao Gao of Qin, Wang Mang of Han, Zhou Yi of Liang, and Lu Shan of Tang. All of them, not following the governance of their former lords and previous emperors, indulged in pleasure, paid no heed to remonstrance, failed to perceive that the realm would fall into disorder, and did not know the sorrows of the people. Thus, before long, they perished.
