# sent_id = sent1.1.1.6
# text = 近く本朝をうかがふに、承平の將門、天慶の純友、康和の義親、平治の信頼、此等はおごれる心もたけき事も皆とりどりにこそありしかども、まぢかくは六波羅の入道、前太政大臣平朝臣清盛公と申し人のありさま、傳へうけたまはるこそ心も詞も及ばれね。
# reading_translation = When I look closely at our own land, Masakado of the Shohei era, Sumitomo of the Tengyo era, Yoshichika of the Kowa era, Nobuyori of the Heiji era—these men, in their pride and their boldness, were each extraordinary in their own way; but more recently, the lay monk of Rokuhara, the former Grand Minister of State, Lord Taira no Kiyomori—the manner of this man, as it has been passed down and received, is beyond the reach of both words and understanding.
# literal_translation = Closely this-land when-I-examine, Shohei's Masakado, Tengyo's Sumitomo, Kowa's Yoshichika, Heiji's Nobuyori, these as-for, proud heart also bold deed also all each-in-their-own-way indeed there-were but, more-recently as-for, Rokuhara's lay-monk, former Grand-Minister-of-State Taira-no-Ason Kiyomori Lord called person's manner, transmitted received as-for, heart also words also cannot-reach.
# transliteration = Chikaku honchō o ukagau ni, shōhei no masakado, tengyō no sumitomo, kōwa no yoshichika, heiji no nobuyori korera ha ogoreru kokoro mo takeki koto mo mina toridorini koso ari shika domo, majikaku ha rokuhara no nyūdō sakinodaijōdaijin tairanoason kiyomori kō to mōshi hito no arisama, tsutae uketamawaru koso kokoro mo kotoba mo oyoba re ne
