# sent_id = sent1.7.1.1
# text = 昔より今に至るまで、源平兩氏朝家に召しつかはれて、王化に隨はず、自朝權を輕んずる者には、互に誡を加しかば、代の亂れもなかりしに、保元に爲義きられ、平治に義朝誅せられて後は、末々の源氏ども、或は流され、或は失はれ、今は平家の一類のみ繁昌して、頭をさし出す者なし。
# reading_translation = From ancient times down to the present, the Minamoto and Taira clans were both summoned to serve the imperial court; and when any of them failed to follow the royal will or made light of the court's authority, they would each in turn inflict punishment upon them, so that there was no disturbance of the age. But after Tameyoshi was executed in the Hōgen era and Yoshitomo was put to death in the Heiji era, the remaining Minamoto of the younger generations were either exiled or killed, and now only the Taira clan flourishes, with no one to raise a head against them.
# literal_translation = From ancient times to the present, Minamoto-Taira both clans to the imperial court were summoned, and, the royal will not following, or the court's authority making light of, those who, mutually punishment inflicted, so the age's disturbance also was not, but, in Hōgen Tameyoshi was executed, in Heiji Yoshitomo was put to death, after that, the remaining Minamoto of the younger generations, some were exiled, some were killed, now only the Taira clan's one family flourishes, and, a head to raise out, person is not.
# transliteration = Mukashi yori ima ni itaru made, genpeiryōshi chōka ni meshitsukaware te, ōka ni shitagawa zu, jichōken o karonzuru mono ni ha, tagaini imashime o kuwashika ba, yo no midare mo nakari shi ni, hōgen ni tameyoshi kirare, heiji ni yoshitomo chūserare te nochi ha, suezue no genji domo, aruiha nagasare, aruiha ushinaware, ima ha heike no ichirui nomi hanjōshi te, kōbe o sashidasu mono nashi.
