# sent_id = sent1.12.5.1
# text = 其比の叙位除目と申は、院内の御はからひにもあらず、攝政關白の御成敗にも及ばず、唯一向平家のまゝにてありしかば、徳大寺、花山院もなり給はず、入道相國の嫡男小松殿、右大將にておはしけるが、左に移りて、次男宗盛、中納言におはせしが、數輩の上臈を超越して、右に加はられけるこそ、申すばかりもなかりしか。
# reading_translation = The appointments to court ranks and offices at that time were not at the discretion of the retired emperor, nor did they come under the authority of the regent or chancellor; they were entirely as the Heike pleased. Thus, even Tokudaiji and Kazan'in were not appointed, and the eldest son of the Lay Monk Chancellor, Lord Komatsu, who was a Major General of the Right, moved to the Left, while the second son, Munemori, who was a Middle Counselor, surpassed many senior nobles and was added to the Right—this was beyond words.
# literal_translation = That time's rank-conferral and office-appointment as-for, retired-emperor's discretion also not-be, regent chancellor's governance also not-reach, solely entirely Heike's as-it-was because, Tokudaiji, Kazan'in also become not, Lay-Monk Chancellor's eldest-son Lord Komatsu, Right Major-General as being, to Left moved, second-son Munemori, Middle Counselor as being, many senior-nobles surpassing, to Right was-added—this, saying even not-was.
# transliteration = Sonokoro no joijimoku to mōsu ha, innai no onhakarai ni mo ara zu, sesshōkanpaku no goseibai ni mo oyoba zu, tattaikkō heike no mama ni te ari shika ba, tokudaiji, kazan'in mo nari tamawa zu, nyūdōshōkoku no chakunan komatsudono, udaishō nite owashi keru ga, hidari ni utsuri te, jinan munemori, chūnagon ni owase shi ga, suhai no jōrō o chōetsu shi te, migi ni kuwawara re keru koso, mōsu bakari mo nakari shika.
# generator = deepseek-v4-pro
