# sent_id = sent1.15.1.1
# text = さる程に山門の大衆、國司加賀守師高を流罪に處せられ、目代近藤判官師經を禁獄せらるべき由、奏聞度々に及ぶといへども、御裁許なかりければ、日吉の祭禮を打ち留めて、安元三年四月十三日辰の一點に、十禪師、客人、八王子三社の神輿かざり奉りて、陣頭へ振奉る。
# reading_translation = Meanwhile, the monks of Enryakuji repeatedly petitioned the court to sentence the provincial governor Kaga no kami Morotaka to exile and to imprison his deputy Kondo no hogan Morotsune, but since no imperial sanction was given, they halted the festival of Hiyoshi and on the thirteenth day of the fourth month of Angen 3, at the hour of the dragon (around 8 a.m.), they decorated the sacred palanquins of the three shrines—Jūzenji, Kyakujin, and Hachioji—and carried them to the imperial palace.
# literal_translation = Such-being-the-case, mountain-gate's great-assembly, provincial-governor Kaga-no-kami Morotaka exile-to sentenced, deputy Kondo-no-hogan Morotsune imprisonment-to should-be, that-effect, petition repeatedly reached though, imperial-sanction not-existed because, Hiyoshi's festival halted, Angen 3 year 4 month 13 day dragon's first-point at, Jūzenji, Kyakujin, Hachioji three-shrines' palanquins decorated, palace-front to brandished.
# transliteration = Saruhodoni sanmon no daishu, kokushi kaganokami morotaka o ruzai ni shoserare, mokudai kondōhangan morotsune o kingoku serarubeki yoshi, sōmon tabitabini oyobu to iedomo, gosaikyo nakarikere ba, hiyoshi no sairei o uchitodomete, angen sannen shigatsu jūsannichi tatsu no itten ni, jūzenji, kyakujin, hachiōji sansha no shin'yo kazari tatematsurite, jintō he furitatematsuru.
