# sent_id = sent2.1.2.2
# text = 八條中納言長方卿、其時はいまだ左大辨宰相にて、末座に候はれけるが、申されけるは、「法家の勘状に任せて、死罪一等を減じて、遠流せらるべしと見えて候へ共、前座主明雲大僧正は、顯密兼學して、淨行持律の上、大乘妙經を公家に授奉り、菩薩淨戒を法皇に持せ奉る。
# reading_translation = The Middle Counselor Nagakata of the Eighth Ward, who was then still the Consultant of the Left Gate Guards, was seated at the lowest seat and said: "According to the judgment of the legal experts, it appears that the death penalty should be reduced by one degree and he should be exiled to a distant land. However, the former head priest Myoun Daisojo, who was learned in both exoteric and esoteric Buddhism, and who, in addition to observing the precepts purely, had bestowed the Mahayana scriptures upon the Emperor and had administered the bodhisattva precepts to the Retired Emperor—
# literal_translation = Eighth-Ward Middle-Counselor Nagakata-lord, at-that-time still Left-Gate-Guards Consultant being, at-lowest-seat was-seated, but, said: "Legal-experts' judgment according-to, death-penalty one-degree reducing, distant-exile should-be-sentenced appears, but, former-head-priest Myoun Great-Bishop, exoteric-esoteric both-learning, pure-conduct keeping-precepts in-addition, Mahayana-wondrous-sutra to-Emperor bestowing, bodhisattva-pure-precepts to-Retired-Emperor administering.
