# reading_translation = When this matter was reported to the new Grand Minister Narichika and his close attendants, and it was heard that the mountain would be attacked, the monks of Enryakuji, harboring resentment against the imperial court, said that they should not disobey the imperial command, and some monks secretly obeyed the retired emperor's decree. The former head priest Myoun Daisojo was staying at Myokobo, and when he heard that the monks were divided in their intentions, he said, "What kind of fate will I meet in the end?"
