# sent_id = sent3.3.3.3
# text = 神社は太神宮を始奉て、二十餘箇所、佛寺は東大寺、興福寺、已下十六箇所に御誦經あり。御誦經の御使は、宮の侍の中に、有官の輩是を勤む。平紋の狩衣に帶劔したる者共が、色々の御誦經物、御劍御衣を持續いて、東の臺より南庭を渡て、西の中門に出づ。
# reading_translation = For the shrines, beginning with the Grand Shrine of Ise, sutra recitations were offered at more than twenty places; for the Buddhist temples, at sixteen places starting with Tōdaiji and Kōfukuji. The imperial messengers for the sutra recitations were chosen from among the courtiers of the palace who held official rank. Men wearing plain-patterned hunting robes and girded with swords carried the various sutra-offering items, the imperial sword and robes, in succession, crossing the southern courtyard from the eastern platform and emerging at the western middle gate.
# literal_translation = Shrines as-for Grand-Shrine as-for beginning-honorably, twenty-odd places, Buddhist-temples as-for Tōdaiji, Kōfukuji, below sixteen places at honorable-sutra-recitation there-was. Honorable-sutra-recitation's honorable-messengers as-for, palace's attendants among, having-rank's people this performed. Plain-pattern's hunting-robes at sword-wearing people, various honorable-sutra-offering-items, honorable-sword honorable-robes carrying-continuing, eastern platform from southern courtyard crossing, western middle-gate to emerged.
# transliteration = Jinja wa daijingū o hajime tatematsuri te nijūyokasho, butsuji wa tōdaiji, kōfukuji, ige jūrokkasho ni gozukyō ari. gozukyō no otsukai wa, miya no saburai no naka ni yūkan no tomogara kore o tsutomu. hiramon no kariginu ni taiken shitaru monodomo ga, iroiro no gozukyōmono, mitsurugi onzo mochitsuzuite, higashi no dai yori nantei o watatte, nishi no chūmon ni izu.
