# text = 修理畢て後、清盛高野へ上り、大塔拜み、奧院へ參られたりければ、何くより來る共なき老僧の、眉には霜を垂れ、額に浪を疊み、鹿杖の兩股なるにすがて、出來給へり。
# reading_translation = After the repairs were completed, Kiyomori went up to Mount Koya, worshipped at the Great Pagoda, and when he visited the Inner Shrine, an old monk, who had come from no one knew where, with frost hanging from his eyebrows and waves of wrinkles on his forehead, leaning on a staff with two prongs like deer antlers, appeared.
# literal_translation = Repairs having been finished after, Kiyomori to Koya went up, Great Pagoda worshipped, Inner Shrine to went when, from where came unknown old monk, eyebrows on frost hung, forehead on waves piled, deer-staff's two-pronged being on leaning, came out.
