# sent_id = sent3.7.1.3
# text = 書置給はすば、爭か是を見るべき。」とて、康頼入道と二人、讀では泣き、泣いては讀む。「安元三年七月廿日出家、同廿六日、信俊下向。」とも書かれたり。さてこそ源左衞門尉信俊が參りたりけるも知れけれ。そばなる壁には、「三尊來迎便有り、九品往生疑なし。」とも書かれたり。此形見を見給てこそ、「さすが欣求淨土の望も御座けり。
# reading_translation = If he had not left this writing, how could we see it?" So saying, he and the priest Yasuyori, the two of them, read it and wept, and wept and read it. "On the twentieth day of the seventh month of Angen 3, I left home; on the twenty-sixth of the same month, Nobutoshi went down to the capital." was also written. It was only then that they knew that Minamoto no Saemon no Jō Nobutoshi had come. On the wall beside it was also written, "There is the coming of the Three Holy Ones to welcome us; there is no doubt of birth in the nine grades of the Pure Land." Seeing this memento, they realized, "Indeed, even he had the aspiration for the Pure Land."
# literal_translation = Writing-left if-not, how this see-should?" saying, Yasuyori-priest with two-people, read-and weep, weep-and read. "Angen-3-year-7-month-20-day leaving-home, same-26-day, Nobutoshi went-down." also was-written. Thereupon indeed Minamoto-no-Saemon-no-Jō-Nobutoshi came had was-known. Beside-being wall-on, "Three-Holy-Ones-coming-to-welcome there-is, nine-grades-birth doubt there-is-not." also was-written. This memento seeing, indeed, "as-expected aspiration-for-Pure-Land also existed."
# transliteration = Kakioki tamawa zuba ikadeka kore o miru beki。」 tote, yasuyorinyūdō to futari, yomide ha naki, nai te ha yomu。「 angen sannen shichigatsu hatsuka shukke, onaji nijūrokunichi, nobutoshi gekō。」 tomo kaka re tari. satekoso minamotonosaemonnojōnobutoshi ga mairi tari keru mo shire kere. sobanaru kabe ni ha、「 sanzonraigō bin ari, kuhon'ōjō utagai nashi。」 tomo kaka re tari. kono katami o mi tamaite koso、「 sasuga gongujōdo no nozomi mo owashikeri.
