# sent_id = sent3.7.3.1
# text = 其後はよもすがら康頼入道と二人、墓の廻を行道して念佛申し、明ぬれば新う壇築き、釘貫せさせ、前に假屋作り、七日七夜、念佛申し經書て結願には大なる卒塔婆を立て、「過去聖靈出離生死、證大菩提」と書て、年號月日の下に、「孝子成經」と書かれたれば、賤山賤の心無も、子に過たる寶はなしとて、涙を流し、袖を絞ぬは無りけり。
# reading_translation = After that, all night long, together with the lay monk Yasuyori, they walked around the grave performing circumambulation and chanting the Buddha's name. When dawn broke, they built a new earthen platform, had stakes driven in, erected a temporary hut in front, and for seven days and seven nights chanted the Buddha's name and recited sutras. At the concluding ceremony, they erected a large stupa and wrote on it: "May the departed spirit leave the cycle of birth and death and attain great enlightenment." Below the year, month, and day, they wrote: "Filial son Naritsune." Even the heartless people of the humble mountain village said, "There is no treasure that surpasses a child," and there was none who did not shed tears and wring their sleeves.
# literal_translation = After that, all night long, Yasuyori the lay monk and two people, around the grave circumambulation doing, Buddha's name chanting, when dawn broke, new platform built, stakes had driven, in front temporary hut built, seven days seven nights, Buddha's name chanting, sutras recited, at the concluding ceremony, large stupa erected, "departed spirit, leaving birth and death, attain great enlightenment" wrote, below year month day, "filial son Naritsune" wrote, so, humble mountain village's heartless people even, "child surpassing treasure there is not" saying, tears shed, sleeves not wringing were none.
# transliteration = Sononochi ha yomosugara yasuyorinyūdō to futari, haka no mawari o gyōdō shite nenbutsu mōshi, akenureba aratau dan kizuki, kuginuki sesase, mae ni kariya tsukuri, shichinichishichiya, nenbutsu mōshi kyōshote kechigan ni ha dainaru sotoba o tate," kakoshōryō shutsurishōji, shōdaibodai" to kaite, nengōgappi no shita ni," kōshinaritsune" to kakaretareba, shizuyamashizu no kokoronashi mo, ko ni sugitaru takara ha nashi tote, namida o nagashi, sode o shiboranu ha nakarikeri.
