# sent_id = sent3.8.2.10
# text = か樣に日の長閑なる時は、磯に出て網人釣人に手を摺り、膝を屈て、魚を貰ひ、汐干の時は貝を拾ひ、荒海布を取り、磯の苔に露の命を懸てこそ、今日までも存たれ。
# reading_translation = In such peaceful days, I would go out to the shore, rub my hands together to beg from net-fishers and anglers, bend my knees, receive fish, gather shells at low tide, collect seaweed from the rough sea, and stake my dew-like life on the moss of the rocks—that is how I have lived until today.
# literal_translation = In-this-way day's peaceful when, to-shore go-out, to-net-fishers-and-anglers hands rub, knees bend, fish receive, low-tide's time shells pick-up, rough-sea seaweed take, on-rock's moss dew's life stake, indeed, until-today have-lived.
# transliteration = Kayōni hi no nodokanaru toki ha, iso ni idete amibito tsuribito ni te o suri, hiza o kagamete, uo o morai, shiohi no toki ha kai o hiroi, arame o tori, iso no koke ni tsuyu no inochi o kakete koso, kyō made mo zonjitare.
