# sent_id = sent3.13.1.2
# text = 毎月十四日十五日を點じて、當家他家の人々の御方より、みめよく若う盛なる女房達を多く請じ聚め、一間に六人づつ、四十八間に二百八十八人、時衆に定て、彼兩日が間は、一心稱名聲斷ず、誠に來迎引攝の悲願も、此所に影向を垂れ、攝取不捨の光も、此大臣を照し給ふかとぞ見えし。
# reading_translation = On the fourteenth and fifteenth of every month, he would light the lamps, and from the households of both his own family and others, he would invite and gather many beautiful, young, and flourishing ladies-in-waiting. In each of the forty-eight rooms, six at a time, making two hundred eighty-eight in all, he appointed them as the assembly of devotees. During those two days, their single-minded invocation of the Buddha's name never ceased. Truly, it seemed that the compassionate vow of the Buddha's descent to welcome and draw in beings manifested itself here, and that the light of never abandoning sentient beings shone upon this minister.
# literal_translation = Every month fourteenth fifteenth (he) lights, own family other family's people's honorable directions from, beautiful young flourishing ladies-in-waiting many invites gathers, one room in six each, forty-eight rooms in two hundred eighty-eight people, assembly of devotees as appointing, those two days' interval, single-minded invocation voice does not cease, truly coming-to-welcome drawing-in's compassionate vow also, this place at manifestation hangs down, receiving-never-abandoning's light also, this minister (object) shines gives (honorific) that it seemed.
# transliteration = Maitsuki jūyokka jūgonichi o tenjite, tōke take no hitobito no onkata yori, mimeyoku wakō sakannaru nyōbōtachi o ōku shōjiatsume, hitoma ni rokunin zutsu, shijūhachiken ni nihyakuhachijūhachinin, jishu ni sadamete, kano ryōjitsu ga aida ha, isshinshōmyō koe taezu, makotoni raigōinjō no higan mo, koko ni yōgō o tare, sesshufusha no hikari mo, konōtodo o terashi tamau ka to zo mie shi.
