# text = 爰を以て古を憶ふに、唐の太宗は魏徴に後て、悲の餘に、『昔の殷宗は夢の中に良弼を得、今の朕は覺ての後賢臣を失ふ。
# reading_translation = Thus, when I recall the past, Emperor Taizong of Tang, after the death of Wei Zheng, in his grief wrote with his own hand an inscription saying, 'The ancient Yin sovereign obtained a good minister in a dream; I, the present emperor, after waking, have lost a worthy subject,' and had it erected at his tomb—how deeply he must have grieved.
# literal_translation = Hereby, when recalling the past, Tang's Taizong, after Wei Zheng, in grief's excess, 'Ancient Yin's sovereign in dream's midst a good minister obtained; now's I, after waking, a worthy subject lost.' saying inscription self-wrote, at tomb erected—how he grieved, it seems.
