# sent_id = sent3.16.1.2
# text = 同十六日入道相國、此日來思立給へる事なれば、關白殿を始奉て、太政大臣以下の公卿、殿上人、四十三人が官職を停て、追籠らる。關白殿をば、太宰帥に遷て、鎭西へ流し奉る。かゝらん世には、とてもかくても有なんとて、鳥羽の邊、古川と云ふ所にて、御出家有り。
# reading_translation = On the same sixteenth day, the Lay Monk Chancellor, since this was a matter he had resolved upon, beginning with the Regent, stripped forty-three nobles—the Grand Minister of State and below, courtiers, and senior officials—of their offices and confined them. The Regent was transferred to the governorship of Dazaifu and exiled to Kyushu. Saying that in such a world it mattered not either way, he took the tonsure at a place called Furukawa in the vicinity of Toba.
# literal_translation = Same sixteenth day, Lay Monk Chancellor, this day having-come-to-resolve matter being, Regent beginning-with, Grand Minister of State and below courtiers, senior officials, forty-three persons' offices stopped, confined. Regent as-for, Dazaifu governor to transferred, Kyushu to exiled. Such world in, either way also be, saying, Toba's vicinity, Furukawa called place at, taking of tonsure there-was.
# transliteration = Dō jūrokunichi nyūdōshōkoku, konohi ki omoitachi tamaeru koto nare ba, kanpakudono o hajime tatematsuri te, daijōdaijin ika no kugyō, tenjōbito, yonjūsannin ga kanshoku o todome te, oikome raru. kanpakudono o ba, dazainosochi ni utsushi te, chinzei he nagashi tatematsuru. kakaran yo ni ha, totemo kakutemo ari nan tote, toba no hotori, furukawa to iu tokoro nite, goshukke ari.
