# reading_translation = Because the Heike were also displeased with him, when it was heard that they would soon come from Rokuhara to seize him, he took his son, E no Saemon no Jō Ienari, and fled without any particular destination. They went up to Inariyama, dismounted from their horses, and the father and son said to each other, "I think we should flee toward the east and rely on the exiled former Hyōe no Suke Yoritomo in Izu Province, but he too is currently a person under imperial censure, and even alone it would be difficult for him to manage."
# literal_translation = This-too Heike heart not-good because, already Rokuhara from press-come seize should as heard while, son E-no-Saemon-no-Jō-Ienari taking-along, where-to also without falling-fled, but Inariyama onto went-up, horse from dismounted, father-child said-to-each-other, "This from east-country direction toward fall-down, Izu-Province's exile former-Hyōe-no-Suke-Yoritomo rely-on should as think though, that-too at-that-time imperial-censure's person being, body-one even manage difficult is."
