# reading_translation = The Prince was composing a poem on the moon seen through a break in the clouds on the night of the fifteenth of the Fifth Month, and had no inkling of what was to come, when a messenger from the lay monk of the Third Rank arrived in haste bearing a letter. The Prince's wet nurse's son, Rokujō no Suke no Tayū Munenobu, took it, brought it before the Prince, and opened it to read: "Your Highness's rebellion has come to light, and they are sending you into exile to the province of Tosa; officials have come to take you into custody.
