# sent_id = sent4.6.6.2
# text = 或時小松殿參内の次に、中宮の御方へ参せ給ひたりけるに、八尺許有ける蛇が、大臣の指貫の左の輪を這廻りけるを、重盛騒がば、女房達も騒ぎ、中宮も驚せ給ひなんずと思召し、左の手で蛇の尾を押へ、右の手で首を取り、直衣の袖の中に引入れ、些ともさわがず、つい立て、「六位や候、六位や候。
# reading_translation = Once, when Lord Komatsu was attending the palace, as he was going to the quarters of the Empress, a snake about eight feet long crawled around the left leg of the Minister's sashinuki. Shigemori thought that if he made a fuss, the court ladies would also make a fuss, and the Empress would be startled. So he pressed the snake's tail with his left hand, took its head with his right hand, drew it into the sleeve of his court robe, and without any disturbance, called out, "Is there a Sixth Rank official? Is there a Sixth Rank official?"
# literal_translation = Once Lord-Komatsu's palace-attendance's occasion, Empress's quarters-to went-honorific-when, eight-feet-about-was snake, Minister's sashinuki's left leg around crawled, Shigemori if-made-fuss, court-ladies also make-fuss, Empress also startled-would-be thought, left hand-with snake's tail pressed, right hand-with head took, court-robe's sleeve-into drew-in, not-at-all without-disturbance, called-out, "Sixth-Rank is-there, Sixth-Rank is-there."
# transliteration = Arutoki komatsudono sandai no tsugi ni, chūgū no onkata he maise tamai tari keru ni, hasshaku bakari ari keru hebi ga, daijin no sashinuki no hidari no wa o haimawari keru o, shigemori sawaga ba, nyōbōtachi mo sawagi, chūgū mo odorokase tamai nan zu to oboshimeshi, hidari no te de hebi no o o osae, migi no te de kubi o tori, nōshi no sode no naka ni hikīre, chittomo sawaga zu, tsuitate," rokui ya sō, rokui ya sō.
