# sent_id = sent4.10.1.2
# text = 大手の大將軍には嫡子伊豆守仲綱、次男源大夫判官兼綱、六條藏人仲家、其子藏人太郎仲光、大衆には圓滿院大輔源覺、成喜院荒土佐、律成房伊賀公、法輪院鬼佐渡、是等は力の強さ、弓箭打物もては、鬼にも神にも逢うと云ふ一人當千の兵也。
# reading_translation = As the great general of the main force, his eldest son Izu no kami Nakatsuna, second son Gen-dayū hōgan Kanetsuna, Rokujō Kurōdo Nakai, his son Kurōdo Tarō Nakamitsu; among the warrior monks, Enman-in Daisuke Gengaku, Jōki-in Aratosā, Risshō-bō Iga no Kō, Hōrin-in Oni-Sado — these men, in strength and with bow, arrow, and striking weapons, were warriors each a match for a thousand, of whom it was said they would meet even demons or gods.
# literal_translation = Main-force's great-general as-for, eldest-son Izu-no-kami Nakatsuna, second-son Gen-dayū-hōgan Kanetsuna, Rokujō-Kurōdo Nakai, his-son Kurōdo-Tarō Nakamitsu, warrior-monks as-for Enman-in-Daisuke Gengaku, Jōki-in-Aratosā, Risshō-bō-Iga-no-Kō, Hōrin-in-Oni-Sado, these as-for strength's strength, bow-arrow striking-weapons with-as-for, demon-to also god-to also meet that say one-match-a-thousand warriors were.
# transliteration = Ōte no daishōgun ni ha chakushi izunokami nakatsuna, jinan gendayūhōgan kanetsuna, rokujōkurōdo nakaie, sono ko kurōdotarō nakamitsu, daishu ni ha enman'indaisukegengaku, jōkīn'aratosa, risshōbōiganokō, hōrin'in'onisado, korera ha chikara no tsuyosa, yumiya uchimono mote ha, oni ni mo kami ni mo au to iu ichinintōsen no tsuwamono nari.
