# sent_id = sent4.10.3.5
# text = 如何が是程の重寶をば左右なうはゑらすべきとて、三井寺の大進僧正覺宗に仰せて、壇上に立て、七日加持して、彫せ給へる御笛也。或時高松中納言實平卿參て、此御笛を吹れけるに、尋常の笛の樣に思忘て、膝より下に置れたりければ、笛や尤けん、其時蝉折にけり。さてこそ蝉折とは付られたれ。笛の御器量たるに依て、此宮御相傳有けり。されども今を限とや思食れけん、金堂の彌勒に參らさせおはします。
# reading_translation = Wondering how he could possibly set aside such a precious treasure, he summoned the high priest Kakushu of Miidera, had him stand on the altar, perform seven days of consecration, and carve it. This is the flute he had made. Once, when the Middle Counselor Takamatsu no Sanesada came and played this flute, he forgot it was an ordinary flute and placed it below his knees, and the flute, as if to say 'how regrettable!', broke at that moment. That is why it was named 'Semi-ori' (Cicada-fold). Because of the flute's excellence, it was passed down in this prince's family. However, thinking perhaps this was the end, he offered it to Maitreya in the Golden Hall.
# literal_translation = How such precious treasure as-for carelessly can-set-aside? saying, Miidera's high priest Kakushu to commanded, on altar made stand, seven days consecration performed, carved gave. This is the flute. Once Takamatsu Middle Counselor Sanesada came, this flute played, ordinary flute's manner as forgot, below knees placed, flute 'how regrettable!' at that time broke. Thus 'Semi-ori' was named. Flute's excellence because, this prince family transmission had. However now as limit thought, Golden Hall's Maitreya to offered.
