# sent_id = sent4.12.4.1
# text = 三位入道七十に餘て軍して、弓手の膝口を射させ、痛手なれば、心靜かに自害せんとて、平等院の門の内へ引退いて、敵おそひかゝりければ、次男源大夫判官兼綱、紺地の錦の直垂に、唐綾威の鎧著て、白葦毛なる馬に乘り、父を延さんと、返合せ／＼防戰ふ。
# reading_translation = Sanmi Nyūdō, over seventy years old, fought, and had his left knee shot; since it was a serious wound, he withdrew inside the gate of Byōdō-in to calmly take his own life. When the enemy attacked, his second son, Gen Daibu Hangan Kanetsuna, wearing a dark blue brocade hitatare and armor laced with Chinese twill, mounted on a white roan horse, turned back again and again to fight, to protect his father.
# literal_translation = Sanmi Nyūdō seventy exceeded and fought, left knee mouth caused to be shot, serious wound because, heart calmly self-kill intending, Byōdō-in's gate's inside into withdrew, enemy attacked when, second son Gen Daibu Hangan Kanetsuna, dark blue brocade's hitatare in, Chinese twill laced armor wearing, white roan horse on rode, father protect intending, turned back again and again fought.
