# sent_id = sent4.16.1.7
# text = 燒る所、本覺院、成喜院、眞如院、花園院、普賢堂、大寶院、清瀧院、教待和尚本坊、竝に本尊等、八間四面の大講堂、鐘樓、經藏、灌頂堂、護法善神の社壇、新熊野の御寶殿、惣じて堂舎塔廟六百三十七宇、大津の在家一千八百五十三宇、智證の渡し給へる一切經七千餘卷、佛像二千餘體、忽に煙と成こそ悲しけれ。
# reading_translation = The places that burned: Hongaku-in, Jōki-in, Shinnyo-in, Hanazono-in, Fugen-dō, Daihō-in, Seiryū-in, the main residence of the monk Kyōtai, and the principal images; the great lecture hall of eight bays by four bays, the bell tower, the sutra repository, the abhisheka hall, the shrine of the guardian deities, the sacred hall of Ima-Kumano; in all, 637 temple buildings and pagodas, 1,853 houses in the town of Ōtsu, over 7,000 scrolls of the complete scriptures that Chishō had transmitted, and over 2,000 Buddhist images—all suddenly turned to smoke, how sorrowful it was!
# literal_translation = Burning place, Hongaku-in, Jōki-in, Shinnyo-in, Hanazono-in, Fugen-dō, Daihō-in, Seiryū-in, Kyōtai-monk main-residence, and principal-images etc., eight-bay-four-bay great-lecture-hall, bell-tower, sutra-repository, abhisheka-hall, guardian-deities' shrine, Ima-Kumano's sacred-hall, in-all temple-buildings-pagodas 637 buildings, Ōtsu's houses 1,853 buildings, Chishō transmitted-gave complete-scriptures 7,000-odd scrolls, Buddhist-images 2,000-odd bodies, suddenly smoke to became, how sorrowful!
# transliteration = Yakeru tokoro, hongakuin, jōkīn, shinnyoin, hanazonoin, fugendō, daihōin, seiryūin, kyōtaioshōhonbō, narabini honzon nado, hachikenshimen no daikōdō, shōrō, kyōzō, kanjōdō, gohōzenshin no shadan, imakumano no gohōden, sōjite dōshatōbyō roppyakusanjūshichiu, ōtsu no zaike issenhappyakugojūsan'u, chishō no watashitamaeru issaikyō shichisen'yokan, butsuzō nisen'yotai, tachimachini kemuri to nari koso kanashikere.
