# sent_id = sent5.1.3.28
# text = 然を桓武天皇、延暦三年十月二日、奈良の京春日の里より、山城國長岡にうつて、十年と云し正月に、大納言藤原小黒丸、參議左大辨紀古佐美、大僧都玄慶等を遣して、當國葛野郡宇多村を見せらるゝに、兩人共に奏して云、此地の體を見るに、左青龍、右白虎、前朱雀、後玄武、四神相應の地なり。
# reading_translation = However, Emperor Kanmu, on the second day of the tenth month of Enryaku 3, moved from Kasuga no Sato in the capital of Nara to Nagaoka in Yamashiro Province, and in the first month of the year called 'ten years', he sent Dainagon Fujiwara no Koguromaru, Sangi Sadaiben Ki no Kosami, Daisozu Genkei and others to inspect Uda Village in Kadono District of that province; both men reported together, saying, 'Looking at the lay of this land, it is a place where the four gods correspond: Blue Dragon on the left, White Tiger on the right, Vermilion Bird in front, Black Tortoise behind.'
# literal_translation = However Emperor-Kanmu, Enryaku-3 year 10th-month 2nd-day, Nara 's capital Kasuga 's village from, Yamashiro-Province Nagaoka to moved, and 10-years called first-month at, Dainagon Fujiwara-no-Koguromaru, Sangi-Sadaiben Ki-no-Kosami, Daisozu Genkei etc. (accusative) sent, this-province Kadono-District Uda-Village (accusative) show (honorific-passive) when, two-people together reported and said, this-land 's condition (accusative) look at, left Blue-Dragon, right White-Tiger, front Vermilion-Bird, behind Black-Tortoise, four-gods corresponding 's land is.
# transliteration = Shika o kanmutennō, enryaku sannen jūgatsu futsuka, nara no kyō kasuga no sato yori, yamashironokuni nagaoka ni utsute, jūnen to ishi shōgatsu ni, dainagon fujiwaranokoguromaru, sangi sadaiben kinokosami, daisōzu genkei ra o tsukawashite, tōgoku kadonogun udamura o mise raruru ni, ryōnin tomoni sōshite ī, konochi no tei o miru ni, hidari seiryū, migi byakko, mae suzaku, ushiro genbu, shijin sōō no chi nari.
