# sent_id = sent5.1.3.31
# text = 昔より代々の帝王、國々所々に、多の都を立てられしかども、かくの如くの勝地は無しとて、桓武天皇殊に執し思食し、大臣公卿諸道の才人等に仰せ合せ、長久なるべき樣とて、土にて八尺の人形を作り、鐡の鎧甲をきせ、同う鐡の弓矢を持せて、東山の嶺に、西向に立てゝ埋まれけり。
# reading_translation = Since ancient times, successive emperors have established many capitals in various provinces and places, but there is no scenic spot like this one, so Emperor Kanmu especially cherished it in his heart, consulted with ministers, nobles, and scholars of various arts, and, saying that it should be everlasting, made a human figure eight shaku tall out of earth, clad it in iron armor, gave it an iron bow and arrows, and buried it standing on the ridge of Higashiyama facing west.
# literal_translation = Since-ancient-times successive-emperors, provinces-places-in, many-capitals established-though, like-this scenic-spot is-not, saying, Emperor-Kanmu especially cherished-thinking, ministers-nobles various-arts' scholars-to consulted, everlasting-should-be-saying, earth-with eight-shaku human-figure made, iron armor-clad, same iron bow-and-arrows-held, Higashiyama's ridge-on, west-facing standing buried.
# transliteration = Mukashi yori daidai no teiō, kunigunitokorodokoro ni, ō no miyako o taterareshikadomo, kakunogotokuno shōchi ha nashi tote, kanmutennō kotoni shūshioboshimeshi, daijinkugyōshodōnosaijintō ni ōseawase, chōkyūnarubekiyō tote, tsuchi nite hasshaku no hitogata o tsukuri, tetsu no gaikō o kise, onajiu tetsu no yumiya o motasete, higashiyama no mine ni, nishimuki ni tatete uzumarekeri.
