# sent_id = sent5.1.4.4
# text = 邂逅に行く人も、小車に乘り、道を歴てこそ通けれ。軒を爭し人のすまひ、日を歴つゝ荒行く。家々は賀茂河桂河に壞入れ、筏に組浮べ、資材雜具舟に積み、福原へと運下す。たゞなりに、花の都、田舎になるこそ哀しけれ。何者の爲態にや有けん。舊き都の内裏の柱に二首の歌をぞ書いたりける。
# reading_translation = Even those who travel by chance ride in small carts and pass along the roads. The dwellings of people who competed for eaves are abandoned day by day and fall into ruin. Houses are broken down and thrown into the Kamo and Katsura rivers, assembled into rafts and floated, with materials and miscellaneous goods loaded onto boats, and transported down to Fukuhara. It is truly sad that the capital of flowers becomes a countryside. What kind of deed was this? On the pillars of the old capital's palace, two poems were written.
# literal_translation = By-chance going people also, small-carts in ride, roads along passing indeed go. Eaves competing people's dwellings, days passing as go to ruin. Houses are Kamo-river Katsura-river into broken-thrown, rafts into assembled floated, materials miscellaneous-goods boats onto loaded, Fukuhara to transported-down. Just as, flower's capital, countryside becoming indeed is sad. What person's deed as was? Old capital's palace's pillars on two poems indeed wrote.
# transliteration = Kaikō ni iku hito mo, oguruma ni nori, michi o hete koso tōkere. noki o arasoishi hito no sumai, hi o hetsutsu areyuku. ieie ha kamogawa katsuragawa ni kowaire, ikada ni kumiukabe, shizaizatsugu fune ni tsumi, fukuhara he to hakobikudasu. tadanarini, hana no miyako, inaka ni naru koso kanashikere. nanimono no shiwaza ni ya ariken. furuki miyako no dairi no hashira ni nishu no uta o zo kaitarikeru.
