# sent_id = sent5.1.5.1
# text = 同き六月九日、新都の事始め有るべしとて、上卿には徳大寺左大將實定卿、土御門宰相中將通親卿、奉行の辨には、藏人左少辨行隆、官人共召具して、和田の松原の西の野を點じて、九條の地を割れけるに、一條より下五條までは其所あて、五條より下は無りけり。
# reading_translation = On the same ninth day of the sixth month, saying that the construction of the new capital should begin, they appointed as the chief official the Middle Counselor Tokudaiji Sanesada, and as the assistant official the Consultant Tsuchimikado Michichika; and as the magistrate, the Chamberlain and Junior Secretary Yukitaka, together with other officials, were summoned, and they marked out the western field of Wada no Matsubara and divided the land of Kujō; from Ichijō down to Gojō the sites were allotted, but below Gojō there was none.
# literal_translation = Same sixth-month ninth-day, new-capital's construction should-be saying, as-chief-official Tokudaiji Left-General Sanesada-Lord, Tsuchimikado Consultant Middle-Counselor Michichika-Lord, as-magistrate's Chamberlain Junior-Secretary Yukitaka, officials together summoned, Wada's pine-grove's west's field marking, Kujō's land divided, Ichijō from below Gojō until those-sites allotted, Gojō from below there-was-not.
# transliteration = Onajiki rokugatsu kokonoka, shinto no kotohajime aru beshi tote, shōkei ni ha tokudaiji sadaishō sanesada kyō, tsuchimikado saishōchūjō michichika kyō, bugyō no ben ni ha, kurōdo sashōben yukitaka, kanjin tomo meshigushite, wada no matsubara no nishi no no o tenjite, kujō no chi o ware keru ni, ichijō yori shimo gojō made ha soko ate, gojō yori shimo ha nashi keri.
