# sent_id = sent5.7.3.15
# text = かくて三七日の大願終に遂げにければ、那智に千日籠り、大峯三度、葛城二度、高野、粉川、金峯山、白山、立山、富士の嶽、伊豆、箱根、信濃の戸隱、出羽の羽黒、惣じて日本國殘る所なく行廻て、さすが猶故郷や戀しかりけん、都へ歸上たりければ、凡そ飛鳥も祈落す程の、やいばの驗者とぞ聞えし。
# reading_translation = Thus, when the great vow of twenty-one days was finally fulfilled, he confined himself at Nachi for a thousand days, went three times to Ōmine, twice to Katsuragi, and also to Kōya, Kokawa, Kinpusen, Hakusan, Tateyama, the peak of Fuji, Izu, Hakone, Shinano's Togakushi, and Dewa's Haguro; in short, he traveled around leaving no place in Japan unvisited, and yet, perhaps still longing for his old home, he returned to the capital. He was renowned as a miracle-worker whose prayers could even bring down flying birds.
# literal_translation = Thus twenty-one-days' great vow finally fulfilled-when, Nachi at thousand-days confined, Ōmine three-times, Katsuragi two-times, Kōya, Kokawa, Kinpusen, Hakusan, Tateyama, Fuji's peak, Izu, Hakone, Shinano's Togakushi, Dewa's Haguro, in short Japan-country remaining-place none traveling-around, and yet still old-home perhaps longed-for, capital to returned-when, about flying-birds even pray-down extent-of, blade's miracle-worker as was-heard.
# transliteration = Kakute sanshichinichi no taigan tsuini toge ni kere ba, nachi ni sennichi komori, ōmine sando, katsuragi nido, kōya, kokawa, kinpusen, hakusan, tateyama, fuji no take, izu, hakone, shinano no togakushi, dewa no haguro, sōjite nihonkoku nokoru tokoro naku yukimegurite, sasuga nao furusato ya koishikari ken, miyako he kaerinoboritari kere ba, oyoso tobutori mo inoriotosu hodo no, yaiba no genja to zo kikoe shi.
