# text = 實にも三日と云に、福原の新都へ上りつゝ前右兵衞督光能卿の許に、聊縁有ければ、其に行いて、「伊豆國の流人、前右兵衞佐頼朝こそ勅勘を許されて、院宣をだにも給はらば、八箇國の家人ども催し集めて、平家を亡し、天下を靜んと申候へ。
# reading_translation = Indeed, on the third day, he went up to the new capital at Fukuhara, and because he had some slight connection with the former Major General of the Right Guards, Lord Mitsuyoshi, he went to his residence and said, "The exile from Izu Province, the former Lieutenant of the Right Guards, Yoritomo, has been pardoned of his imperial censure, and if he could but receive an imperial decree, he would summon the warriors of eight provinces, destroy the Heike, and pacify the realm."
# literal_translation = Truly, third day when, Fukuhara's new capital to went up, former Right Guards' Major General Mitsuyoshi Lord's place to, slight connection there-was because, there went, "Izu Province's exile, former Right Guards' Lieutenant Yoritomo indeed imperial censure has been pardoned, imperial decree even if receive, eight provinces' warriors summon, Heike destroy, realm pacify would like to say."
# transliteration = Jitsu ni mo mikka to iu ni, fukuhara no shinto he nobori tsutsu sakinōhyōenokami mitsuyoshikyō no moto ni, isasaka en are ba, soko ni okonai te," izunokuni no runin, sakinōhyōenosuke yoritomo koso chokkan o yurusare te, inzen o dani mo tamawa ba, hakkakoku no kenin domo moyōshi atsume te, heike o horoboshi, tenka o shizun to mōshi sōrae.
