# reading_translation = On the next day, when they had decided to exchange arrows at the Fuji River between the Genji and the Heike, as night fell, when the Heike side looked out over the Genji camp, they saw the fires of the encampments of the people and peasants of Izu and Suruga, who, fearing the battle, had either gone into the fields and hidden in the mountains, or boarded boats and floated on the sea and rivers. The Heike warriors said, "Oh, how numerous are the distant fires of the Genji camp!"
# literal_translation = Tomorrow, Genji-Heike at-Fuji-River, arrow-exchange as had-decided, into-night entering, from-Heike-side Genji's camp when-looked-over, Izu-Suruga's people-peasants etc., battle fearing, some into-fields entered mountains hid, some onto-boats boarded, sea-rivers floated, camp's fires were-visible, Heike's warriors "Oh how-numerous Genji's camp's distant-fires' manyness!"
