# text = 東大寺は常在不滅、實報寂光の生身の御佛と思めし準へて、聖武皇帝、手ら親ら琢き立給ひし金銅十六丈の盧舎那佛、鳥瑟高く顯れて、半天の雲にかくれ、白毫新に拜れ給ひし滿月の尊容も、御頭は燒落て大地に有り、御身は鎔合て山の如し。
# reading_translation = Todaiji was thought to be eternal and indestructible, the living body of the Buddha in the Land of Actual Reward and Tranquil Light. Emperor Shomu himself carved and erected the sixteen-jō gilt-bronze statue of Vairocana. Its ushnisha rose high, hidden among the clouds of mid-sky; its white curl between the eyebrows, the full-moon countenance newly worshipped, also—its head burned off and lies on the ground, its body melted together like a mountain.
# literal_translation = Todaiji as-for eternal-indestructible, Actual-Reward-Tranquil-Light's living-body's Buddha as thought, Emperor-Shomu, own-hand personally carved-erected gilt-bronze sixteen-jō's Vairocana-Buddha, ushnisha high appeared, half-sky's clouds-in hidden, white-curl newly worshipped full-moon's venerable-countenance also, head burned-off ground-in is, body melted-together mountain like.
