# sent_id = sent6.1.4.3
# text = 上皇は、去去年法皇の鳥羽殿におしこめられさせ給し御事、去年高倉宮の討たれさせ給し御有樣、都遷とて淺間しかりし天下の亂れ、加樣の事共御心苦しう思食されけるより御惱つかせ給ひて、常は煩しう聞えさせ給ひしが、東大寺興福寺の亡びぬるよし聞召されて、御惱彌重らせ給ふ。
# reading_translation = The Retired Emperor, because he had been grieved in his heart by such events as the matter of the Cloistered Emperor's having been confined in the Toba Palace two years before, the sight of Prince Takakura's having been killed the previous year, and the disturbance of the realm when the capital was moved—an ignominious affair—fell ill, and although he had always been in poor health, when he heard that the Tōdaiji and Kōfukuji temples had been destroyed, his illness grew all the more severe.
# literal_translation = Retired-Emperor, as-for, two-years-ago Cloistered-Emperor's Toba-Palace-in confined-honorific-causative-honorific-past matter, last-year Prince-Takakura's killed-honorific-past sight, capital-moving as ignominious-past realm's disturbance, such matters heart-painful thinking-honorific-past from illness-honorific-past, always as-for ill-honorific-past but, Tōdaiji-Kōfukuji's destroyed-past report hearing-honorific-past, illness more-and-more severe-honorific-present.
# transliteration = Jōkō wa, kozokozo hōō no tobadono ni oshikomerare sase tamai shi onkoto, kozo takakuranomiya no utare sase tamai shi on'arisama, miyakōtsuri tote asamashikari shi tenka no midare, kayō no kotodomo onkokorogurushū oboshimesare keru yori onnō tsukase tamai te, tsune wa wazurawashū kikoesase tamai shi ga, tōdaiji kōfukuji no horobi nuru yoshi kikoshimesare te, onnō iyoiyōmorase tamau.
