# sent_id = sent6.4.7.17
# text = 入道相國の餘に怖き事をのみ申すと聞しかば淺ましさに、内裏をばにげ出て、此程はかゝる栖ひなれば、琴など彈く事無りつれども、さても有るべきならねば、明日よりは大原の奥に思ひ立つ事の候へば、主の女房の今夜ばかりの名殘を惜うで、今は夜も更ぬ、立聞く人もあらじなど勸れば、さぞな昔の名殘もさすが床くて、手馴し琴を彈く程に、安うも聞出されけりな。
# reading_translation = When I heard that the Chancellor was saying nothing but terrifying things, I was so shocked that I fled from the palace. Since I have been living in such a place as this, I have not played the koto or anything, but as it cannot be helped, from tomorrow I intend to go deep into Ohara. The lady of the house, lamenting that this is the last night, urged me, saying, 'The night is already late, and there will be no one listening,' so, indeed, even the memories of the past are moving, and as I played the koto I was accustomed to, I was heard playing it with ease.
# literal_translation = Chancellor's too terrifying things only says when heard, in shock, palace fled, this while such dwelling is, koto etc. playing thing was not, but even so should be not, from tomorrow Ohara's depths intend thing is, mistress's tonight only's regret lamenting, now night also has deepened, standing listening person also will not be, etc. urged, so indeed past's regret also as expected moving, accustomed koto playing while, easily was heard.
# transliteration = Nyūdōshōkoku no amarini osoroshiki koto o nomi mōsu to kikishikaba asamashisa ni, dairi oba nigeidete, konohodo ha kakaru sumika nareba, koto nado hiku koto nakaritsuredomo, satemo arubeki naraneba, asu yori ha ōhara no oku ni omohitatsu koto no saburaheba, aruji no nyōbō no kon'ya bakari no nagori o oshiude, ima ha yo mo fukenu, tachikiku hito mo araji nado susumereba, sazona mukashi no nagori mo sasuga yukashikute, tenarashi koto o hiku hodoni, yasūmo kikīdasarekerina.
