# sent_id = sent6.11.2.3
# text = 昌泰の比ほひ、寛平法皇、大井河へ御幸在しに、勸修寺の内大臣高藤公の御子、泉の大將貞國、小倉山の嵐に烏帽子を河へ吹入られ袖にて髻を押へ、爲方なくてぞ立たりけるに、此如無僧都三衣箱の中より烏帽子一つとり出されたるけるとかや。
# reading_translation = In the Shōtai era, when Emperor Kōkō made an imperial visit to the Ōi River, the son of the Inner Minister of Kanjūji, Lord Takafuji, the General of Izumi, Sadakuni, had his eboshi blown into the river by the wind from Mount Ogura, and holding his topknot with his sleeve, he stood there helplessly, when this Nyomu Sozu took out an eboshi from his robe box, it is said.
# literal_translation = Shōtai's time, Kōkō Retired Emperor, Ōi River to imperial visit was, Kanjūji's Inner Minister Takafuji Lord's son, Izumi's General Sadakuni, Ogura Mountain's wind by eboshi into river blown, sleeve with topknot held, helplessly stood, this Nyomu Sozu robe box from eboshi one took out, it is said.
# transliteration = Shōtai no korōi, kanpyōhōō, ōigawa e gokō mashi ni, kanjuji no naidaijin takafujikō no miko, izumi no taishō sadakuni, ogurayama no arashi ni eboshi o kawa e fukīrerare sode nite motodori o osae, shikata nakute zo tachi tari keru ni, kono nyomusōzu san'ebako no naka yori eboshi hitotsu toridasare taru keru tokaya.
