# sent_id = sent6.11.2.4
# text = 彼僧都は、父、山蔭中納言、太宰大貳に成て鎭西へ下られける時、二歳なりしを、繼母惡であからさまに抱くやうにして、海に落し入殺さんとしけるを、死にける誠の母、存生の時、桂の鵜飼が鵜の餌にせんとて、龜を取て殺さんとしけるを著給へる小袖を脱ぎ、龜にかへ、放たれたりしが、其恩を報ぜんと、此若君落し入けるを水の上に浮び來て、甲に乘てぞ扶けたりける。
# reading_translation = When that monk's father, the Middle Counselor Yamakage, was appointed Dazai no Daini and went down to Kyushu, the boy was two years old. His stepmother, out of malice, pretended to embrace him and tried to throw him into the sea to kill him. But his real mother, who had died, had once, while alive, taken off the small-sleeved robe she was wearing and exchanged it for a turtle that a cormorant fisherman of Katsura was about to kill to use as food for his cormorants, and released the turtle. To repay that kindness, the turtle rose to the surface of the water with the young lord on its shell and saved him.
# literal_translation = That monk, father, Yamakage Middle Counselor, Dazai no Daini became and to Kyushu went down when, two years old was, stepmother out of malice openly as if embracing, into sea threw in and tried to kill, but died real mother, while alive, Katsura's cormorant fisherman's cormorant's food to make, turtle took and tried to kill, wearing small-sleeved robe took off, turtle exchanged, released, that kindness to repay, this young lord threw in, on water floated came, on shell riding saved.
# transliteration = Kano sōzu ha, chichi, yamakagechūnagon, dazainodaini ni natte chinzei he kudararekeru toki, nisai narishi o, mamahaha aku deakarasamani idaku yōnishite, umi ni otoshīre korosantoshikeru o, shinikeru makotonohaha, zonshōnotoki, katsuranōkaigaunoenisentote, kame o totte korosantoshikeru o kisetamaeru kosode o nugi, kame nikae, hanataretarishi ga, sonōn o hōzento, konowakagimi otoshīrekeru o mizunōeni ukabikite, kōninotte zo tasuketarikeru.
