# sent_id = sent6.12.1.2
# text = 朝恩の忝さに、木曽追討の爲に、都合三萬餘騎同六月十五日門出して、明る十六日の卯刻にすでに討立んとしけるに、夜半許、俄に大風吹き、大雨降り、雷おびたゞしう鳴て、天晴て後雲井に大なる聲のしはがれたるを以て、「南閻浮提金銅十六丈の盧遮那佛燒亡し奉る平家の方人する者爰に有り、召取や。
# reading_translation = Grateful for the imperial favor, for the purpose of hunting down Kiso, he set out on the fifteenth day of the sixth month with a force of over thirty thousand horsemen, and at dawn on the sixteenth, just as he was about to depart, around midnight a great wind suddenly blew, heavy rain fell, and thunder roared violently; after the sky cleared, a great hoarse voice from the clouds said, "Here is one who sides with the Heike, who have burned down the sixteen-foot gilt-bronze statue of Vairocana Buddha of Jambudvipa. Seize him!"
# literal_translation = Imperial-favor's gratitude-in, Kiso-hunting's purpose-for, total thirty-thousand-odd horsemen same sixth-month fifteenth-day departure-doing, bright sixteenth-day's dawn-hour-at already depart-about-to-do-when, midnight-about, suddenly great-wind blew, heavy-rain fell, thunder violently roared, sky-cleared-after clouds-in great voice's hoarse-one with, "Jambudvipa gilt-bronze sixteen-foot's Vairocana-Buddha burned-down-humbly Heike's side-person-doing person here is, seize!"
# transliteration = Chōon no katajikenasa ni, kisotsuitō no tame ni, tsugō sanman'yoki dō rokugatsu jūgonichi kadode shite, akaru jūrokunichi no unokoku ni sudeni utatan to shi keru ni, yohan bakari, niwakani ōkaze fuki, ōame furi, kaminari obitadashiku natte, ten harete nochi kumoi ni dainaru koe no shiwagaretaru o motte," nan'enbudai kondō jūrokujō no rushanabutsu shōbōshi tatematsuru heike no kataudo suru mono kokoni ari, meshitore ya.
