# sent_id = sent7.2.1.6
# text = 大將軍には小松三位中將維盛、越前三位通盛、但馬守經正、薩摩守忠度、參河守知度、淡路守清房、侍大將には、越中前司盛俊、上總大夫判官忠綱、飛騨大夫判官景高、高橋判官長綱、河内判官秀國、武藏三郎左衞門有國、越中二郎兵衞盛嗣、上總五郎兵衞忠光、惡七兵衞景清を先として、以上大將軍六人、しかるべき侍三百四十餘人、都合其勢十萬餘騎、壽永二年四月十七日辰の一點に都を立て、北國へこそ趣きけれ。
# reading_translation = As the great generals, they appointed Komatsu no Sanmi Chūjō Koremori, Echizen no Sanmi Michimori, Tajima no Kami Tsunemasa, Satsuma no Kami Tadanori, Mikawa no Kami Tomonori, Awaji no Kami Kiyofusa; as the samurai commanders, they appointed Etchū no Zenji Moritoshi, Kazusa no Daibu Hōgan Tadatsuna, Hida no Daibu Hōgan Kagetaka, Takahashi Hōgan Naganori, Kawachi Hōgan Hidekuni, Musashi Saburō Saemon no Jō Arikuni, Etchū Jirō Hyōe Moritsugu, Kazusa Gorō Hyōe Tadamitsu, and Aku Shichibyōe Kagekiyo as the vanguard. In total, there were six great generals, about three hundred and forty worthy samurai, and altogether their force numbered more than one hundred thousand horsemen. On the seventeenth day of the fourth month of the second year of Juei, at the hour of the dragon (around 8 a.m.), they departed the capital and headed toward the northern provinces.
# literal_translation = As great generals, Komatsu-no-Sanmi-Chūjō Koremori, Echizen-no-Sanmi Michimori, Tajima-no-Kami Tsunemasa, Satsuma-no-Kami Tadanori, Mikawa-no-Kami Tomonori, Awaji-no-Kami Kiyofusa; as samurai commanders, Etchū-no-Zenji Moritoshi, Kazusa-no-Daibu-Hōgan Tadatsuna, Hida-no-Daibu-Hōgan Kagetaka, Takahashi-Hōgan Naganori, Kawachi-Hōgan Hidekuni, Musashi-Saburō-Saemon-no-Jō Arikuni, Etchū-Jirō-Hyōe Moritsugu, Kazusa-Gorō-Hyōe Tadamitsu, Aku-Shichibyōe Kagekiyo as vanguard; in total great generals six, worthy samurai three hundred forty-some, altogether their force one hundred thousand-some horsemen, Juei second year fourth month seventeenth day dragon's first point at capital [acc] departed, toward northern provinces indeed headed.
# transliteration = Taishōgun ni ha komatsunosanmichūjōkoremori, echizennosanmimichimori, tajimanokamitsunemasa, satsumanokamitadanori, mikawanokamitomonori, awajinokamikiyofusa, samuraidaishō ni ha, etchūnozenjimoritoshi, kazusanotaifuhōgantadatsuna, hidanotaifuhōgankagetaka, takahashihōgannaganori, kawachihōganhidekuni, musashisaburōsaemonnojōarikuni, etchūjirōhyōemoritsugu, kazusagorōhyōetadamitsu, akushichibyōekagekiyo o saki to shite, ijō taishōgun rokunin, shikarubeki samurai sanbyakuyonjūyonin, tsugō sonosei jūman'yoki, jueininen shigatsujūshichinichi tatsunoitten ni miyako o tate, hokkoku he koso omomuki kere.
