# sent_id = sent7.9.2.2
# text = 大神宮は高天原より天降せ給ひしを垂仁天皇の御宇、廿五年三月に、大和國笠縫の里より、伊勢國渡會の郡、五十鈴の河上、下津磐根に大宮柱をふとしきたて、祝初奉てより以降、日本六十餘州、三千七百五十餘社の、大小の神祗冥道の中には無雙也。
# reading_translation = The Grand Shrine of Ise, which descended from Takamagahara, was first established in the 25th year, 3rd month of the reign of Emperor Suinin, when the great pillar was firmly planted at the lower rock base on the upper reaches of the Isuzu River in Watarai District, Ise Province, from the village of Kasanui in Yamato Province. Since the first offering of prayers, among the great and small deities and the unseen realms of the more than 3,750 shrines in the sixty-odd provinces of Japan, it is without peer.
# literal_translation = Grand Shrine as-for Takamagahara from descended-honorably, Suinin Emperor's reign, 25th year 3rd month in, Yamato Province Kasanui village from, Ise Province Watarai district, Isuzu river upper reaches, lower rock base at great pillar firmly planted, first offering made since, Japan sixty-odd provinces, 3,750-odd shrines', great and small deities unseen realms among, peerless is.
# transliteration = Daijingū wa takamagahara yori amakudase tamai shi o suinintennō no gyō, nijūgonen sangatsu ni, yamatokoku kasanui no sato yori, isekoku watarai no gun, isuzu no kawakami, shimotsuiwane ni ōmiyabashira o futoshikitate, iwaihajimematsurite yori ikō, nihon rokujūyoshū, sanzennanahyakugojūyosha no, daishō no jingimeidō no naka ni wa musō nari
