# reading_translation = However, although there had been no imperial visits in successive reigns, in the time of Emperor Nara there was a man called Fujiwara no Hirotsugu, who was the grandson of the Minister of the Left Fuhito, the son of the Consultant and Minister of Ceremonial Utsugu, and held the offices of Junior Captain of the Right Inner Palace Guards and Assistant Governor-General of Dazaifu.
